    "title": "Peake Challenge to be held Feb. 10",
    "date": "2024-01-11",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Peake Challenge to be held Feb. 10\n\n January 11, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: News \n \n 152\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n Peake Challengeto be held Feb. 10\nWYE MILLS — The schedule for the annual Bayside Basketball Peake Challenge at Chesapeake College on Saturday, Feb. 10, has been released.\nThe lone girls game will pit St. Michaels against Mardela in the main gymnasium at 11 a.m.\nSix boys varsity games are scheduled for the main gym, with St. Michaels playing Mardela at 12:30 p.m., followed by Queen Anne's-Wicomico (2 p.m.); North Caroline-Parkside (3:30 p.m.); Kent County-Pocomoke (5:30 p.m.); Colonel Richardson-Crisfield (7 p.m.); and Easton-James M. Bennett (8:30).\nFive boys junior varsity games are slated for the school's auxiliary gym, starting with Queen Anne's vs. Wicomico (12:30 p.m.), followed by North Caroline-Parkside (2 p.m.); Kent County-Pocomoke (3:30 p.m.); Colonel Richardson-Crisfield (5:30 p.m.); and Easton-J.M. Bennett at 7 p.m.\nAll-day passes for all games are $10 for adults, $5 for students. No state, county, school or coaching passes will be honored. For more information, contact Frank Szymanski at 410-822-5400. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 1,
    "day": 11,
    "metadata_sport": "basketball",
    "metadata_story_type": "preview",
    "metadata_location": "Wye Mills, Maryland",
    "metadata_teams": "[\"St. Michaels\", \"Mardela\", \"Queen Anne's\", \"Wicomico\", \"North Caroline\", \"Parkside\", \"Kent County\", \"Pocomoke\", \"Colonel Richardson\", \"Crisfield\", \"Easton\", \"James M. Bennett\"]",
