  {
    "title": "Easton's Weems wins 200-free title",
    "date": "2024-02-24",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Easton's Weems wins 200-free title\n\n February 24, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 93\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n COLLEGE PARK — Easton High sophomore Maddie Weems won the girls 200-yard freestyle Saturday during the Class 3A/2A/1A state swimming championships at the University of Maryland's Eppley Recreation Center.Weems clocked a first-place time of 1 minute, 54.53 seconds, outdistancing Damascus freshman Taya Ivanovskaya (1:58.06).\nWeems was the only Bayside swimmer to win a state title Saturday.\nKent Island freshman Clare O'Keefe finished second in the girls 50 freestyle, touching the wall in 24.82. La Plata junior Jadyn Woolsey was first in 23.88.\nA complete story will appear in a later edition of The Star Democrat. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 2,
